window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-345f9e63361a6444"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-in-slack\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"slack-chatgpt\">在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 Slack 频道中提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 即可发起请求。如果你的工作区启用了云端委派，ChatGPT 可以将仓库工作交给单独的 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud</a> 任务处理，并将结果返回到该讨论串。</p> <p><strong>致工作区管理员：</strong>有关应用设置、工作区连接和访问控制，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">在 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams 中设置和管理 @ChatGPT</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-slack-app\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack\">设置 Slack 应用</h2> <p>ChatGPT 工作区所有者或管理员负责设置工作区的 Slack 部署。具体可用的控制项取决于工作区启用的功能。</p> <p>如果你看不到这些控制项，请询问 ChatGPT 工作区管理员，确认是否可以使用 Slack 部署。你所在 Slack 工作区的应用政策也同样适用。</p> <p>工作区必须提供云端委派功能，并且需要有一个已发布且与工作区共享的环境。请管理员按照<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\">为 Slack 启用 Codex Cloud</a>中的说明操作。如果 Codex Cloud 启用了基于角色的访问控制（RBAC），部署所用的服务账户和你的账户都需要拥有 Codex Cloud 访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-your-account-when-prompted\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">按提示连接账户</h3> <p>工作区设置和个人账户连接是两个独立步骤。如果 ChatGPT 要求你先连接账户再继续：</p> <ol> <li>选择 Slack 消息中的连接链接；如果出现提示，请登录。</li> <li>连接你发起请求的同一个工作区中的 Slack。</li> <li>返回原来的 Slack 讨论串，再次提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 重试。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"start-a-task\"></a> <a id=\"start-a-chat\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-request\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">发起请求</h2> <ol> <li>在已启用应用的频道中提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code>，并说明你希望得到什么结果。如果是编程任务，请提供仓库名称和讨论串中的相关上下文。</li> <li>完成账户连接或审批提示。批准之前，请检查任务内容和所需访问权限。</li> <li>要继续处理相关请求，请留在同一讨论串中并再次提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code>。</li> </ol> <p>例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT investigate the failing checkout tests in acme/storefront and propose a fix.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：@ChatGPT，请调查 acme/storefront 中失败的结账测试，并提出修复方案。</p> </blockquote> <p>然后在该讨论串中继续提出要求：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT add a regression test for the fix and summarize the checks you ran.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：@ChatGPT，请为这个修复补充回归测试，并总结你执行了哪些检查。</p> </blockquote> <p>请在工作区启用的公开或私有频道中使用此功能。此工作流不支持与其他组织共享的 Slack Connect 频道。</p> <p><a id=\"how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"run-repository-work-in-codex-cloud\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cloud\">在 Codex Cloud 中运行仓库任务</h2> <p>云端委派需要符合条件、与工作区共享且已发布的环境。对于 Enterprise 工作区，请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">云环境指南</a>准备并发布经过测试的设置，并遵循<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">在 Enterprise 工作区内共享环境</a>的说明。请确认该环境可用于请求中指定的仓库。</p> <ul> <li><strong>环境选择：</strong>ChatGPT 会从你有权访问的工作区共享云环境中选择。使用你的账户时，它会在开始前确认你有权访问该环境。个人云环境不会包含在候选中。在请求中写明仓库或共享环境名称，有助于 ChatGPT 正确选择。</li> <li><strong>独立编程任务：</strong>仓库工作会使用你的账户在独立任务中运行。你需要有权访问所选环境，也需要有权访问任何要求身份验证的仓库。</li> <li><strong>后续工作：</strong>同一 Slack 讨论串中的相关请求可以继续使用原来的编程任务和环境，前提是运行任务时使用同一个账户。使用其他账户发起的请求可能会创建单独的编程任务。如果需要换用其他环境，请开始新的对话。</li> </ul> <p>共享环境不会授予他人访问仓库的权限，也不会共享你的个人凭据值。共享之前，请查看环境中由环境所有者设置的<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">值和预置文件</a>，因为使用该环境的人可能可以访问这些内容。</p> <p>如果没有符合条件的共享环境，请先解决环境或访问权限问题再重试。有关服务访问，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">连接服务</a>以及<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">环境变量和网络机密</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"enterprise-data-controls\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"review-approvals-and-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">检查审批和结果</h2> <p>如果请求需要你授权，ChatGPT 可能会显示包含 <strong>Allow（允许）</strong>和 <strong>Deny（拒绝）</strong>控件的私密审批卡片。作出决定前，请检查任务分配内容以及可供选择的环境。</p> <p>任务开始时，ChatGPT 可能会在原讨论串中发布消息。如果提供 <strong>Follow along（跟踪进度）</strong>和 <strong>Cancel（取消）</strong>控件，它们只会显示给请求者。使用 <strong>Follow along</strong> 打开任务并检查执行情况；频道回复不会让频道中的每个人都能访问底层任务。</p> <p>ChatGPT 会将结果返回到讨论串。使用或合并结果之前，请检查答复、变更和报告中的检查结果。在讨论串中提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code>，即可要求更正或继续处理。</p> <p><a id=\"data-usage-privacy-and-security\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">数据使用、隐私和安全</h2> <p>发布到 Slack 频道的回复可被有权访问该频道的人阅读。请要求 ChatGPT 只分享适合该受众的信息。私密审批卡片不会让之后发布到频道的回复也变成私密内容。</p> <p>不要在 Slack 提示中填写机密信息；处理仓库工作时请使用环境的凭据控制。请查看 <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=security-faq\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">部署访问边界（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>，并遵守工作区的数据和应用政策。</p> <p><a id=\"move-to-the-chatgpt-app\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">切换到 ChatGPT 应用</h2> <p>如果你以前使用 <code>@Codex</code>，请在管理员启用 ChatGPT 应用后用 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 发起新请求。按照提示完成账户连接和审批。</p> <p><a id=\"tips-and-troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">提示与故障排查</h2> <ul> <li><strong>没有回复：</strong>确认频道已启用 ChatGPT，并明确提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code>。请使用组织内部的频道，不要使用 Slack Connect 频道。</li> <li><strong>再次要求连接账户：</strong>检查 ChatGPT 是否已连接到你正在发起请求的 Slack 工作区，然后在同一讨论串中重试。</li> <li><strong>没有符合条件的云环境：</strong>确认环境已发布并与工作区共享，且运行任务的账户拥有所需访问权限。个人云环境不会出现在此工作流中。</li> <li><strong>无法启动编程任务：</strong>请管理员确认工作区已提供云端委派并启用 Codex Cloud。如果 Codex Cloud 启用了基于角色的访问控制，请检查部署所用的服务账户和你的账户是否都拥有 Codex Cloud 访问权限。也请确认你有权访问所选环境及其仓库。</li> <li><strong>需要换用其他环境：</strong>开始新的对话，并写明所需的仓库或共享环境。</li> <li><strong>看不到任务控件：</strong>是否提供 <strong>Follow along</strong>和 <strong>Cancel</strong>取决于部署配置；这些控件供请求者使用。</li> <li><strong>讨论串很长：</strong>在最新请求中概述相关问题、预期结果和仓库信息，确保任务拥有足够上下文。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-chatgpt-in-slack\">Use ChatGPT in Slack</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> in a Slack channel to start a request. If your workspace has Cloud delegation enabled, ChatGPT can send repository work to a separate <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud</a> task and return the result to the thread.</p> <p><strong>For workspace admins:</strong> See <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Set up and manage @ChatGPT in Slack and Microsoft Teams</a> for app setup, workspace connections, and access controls.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-the-slack-app\">Set up the Slack app</h2> <p>A ChatGPT workspace owner or admin sets up the workspace's Slack deployment. The available controls depend on your workspace's enabled features.</p> <p>If you don't see these controls, ask your ChatGPT workspace admin whether Slack deployments are available. Your Slack workspace's app policies also apply.</p> <p>Cloud delegation must be available in your workspace and requires a published environment shared with the workspace. Ask your admin to <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\">enable Codex Cloud for Slack</a>. Where Codex Cloud role-based access control is enabled, both the deployment's service account and your account need Codex Cloud access.</p> <h3 id=\"connect-your-account-when-prompted\">Connect your account when prompted</h3> <p>Workspace setup and your personal account connection are separate. If ChatGPT asks you to connect your account before continuing:</p> <ol> <li>Select the connection link in the Slack message and sign in if prompted.</li> <li>Connect Slack for the same workspace where you made the request.</li> <li>Return to the original Slack thread and mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> to retry.</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"start-a-task\"></a> <a id=\"start-a-chat\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"start-a-request\">Start a request</h2> <ol> <li>In a channel where the app is enabled, mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> and describe the result you want. For coding work, include the repository and relevant context from the thread.</li> <li>Complete any account-connection or approval prompts. Review the requested work and access before you approve.</li> <li>Continue related requests in the same thread, mentioning <code>@ChatGPT</code> again.</li> </ol> <p>For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT investigate the failing checkout tests in acme/storefront and propose a fix.\n</code></pre> <p>Then follow up in that thread:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@ChatGPT add a regression test for the fix and summarize the checks you ran.\n</code></pre> <p>Use an enabled public or private channel in your workspace. Slack Connect channels shared with another organization aren't supported by this flow.</p> <p><a id=\"how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"run-repository-work-in-codex-cloud\">Run repository work in Codex Cloud</h2> <p>Cloud delegation requires an eligible workspace-shared environment with a published version. For an Enterprise workspace, prepare and publish a tested setup using the <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">cloud environment guide</a> and follow the guidance to <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">share it within your Enterprise workspace</a>. Confirm that the environment is available for the requested repository.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Environment selection</strong>: ChatGPT selects from accessible workspace-shared Cloud environments. When using your account, it checks that you can access the environment before starting. Personal Cloud environments aren't included. Name the repository or shared environment in your request to help ChatGPT choose.</li> <li><strong>Separate coding task</strong>: Repository work runs in a separate task using your account. You need access to the selected environment and to any repositories that require authentication.</li> <li><strong>Follow-up work</strong>: Related requests in the same Slack thread can continue the coding task and environment when they use the same account to run it. A request using another account may start a separate coding task. Start a new conversation when you need a different environment.</li> </ul> <p>Sharing an environment doesn't grant repository access or share your personal credential values. Review its <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">environment-owned values and prepared files</a> before sharing, because those can be available to people who use the environment.</p> <p>If no eligible shared environment is available, resolve the environment or access issue before retrying. For service access, see <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">Connect to services</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">Environment variables and network secrets</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"enterprise-data-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"review-approvals-and-results\">Review approvals and results</h2> <p>When a request needs your authorization, ChatGPT can show a private approval card with <strong>Allow</strong> and <strong>Deny</strong> controls. Review the assignment and any available environment choice before deciding.</p> <p>ChatGPT can post a message in the original thread when the task starts. When the <strong>Follow along</strong> and <strong>Cancel</strong> controls are available, they appear for the requester. Use <strong>Follow along</strong> to open the task and inspect its work; the channel reply doesn't give every channel member access to the underlying task.</p> <p>ChatGPT returns the result to the thread. Review the answer, changes, and reported checks before using or merging it. Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> in the thread to request a correction or follow-up.</p> <h2 id=\"data-usage-privacy-and-security\">Data usage, privacy, and security</h2> <p>A response posted to a Slack channel can be read by people with access to that channel. Ask ChatGPT to share only information appropriate for that audience. A private approval card doesn't make the resulting channel reply private.</p> <p>Keep secrets out of Slack prompts and use the environment's credential controls for repository work. Review <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=security-faq\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">deployment access boundaries (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>, and follow your workspace's data and app policies.</p> <h2 id=\"move-to-the-chatgpt-app\">Move to the ChatGPT app</h2> <p>If you previously used <code>@Codex</code>, start new requests with <code>@ChatGPT</code> after your admin enables the ChatGPT app. Follow any connection and approval prompts.</p> <h2 id=\"tips-and-troubleshooting\">Tips and troubleshooting</h2> <ul> <li><strong>No response</strong>: Confirm that ChatGPT is enabled for the channel and mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> explicitly. Use a channel within your organization rather than a Slack Connect channel.</li> <li><strong>Account connection requested again</strong>: Check that you connected ChatGPT to the Slack workspace where you're making the request, then retry in the same thread.</li> <li><strong>No eligible Cloud environment</strong>: Check that the environment is published and shared with the workspace, and that the account running the task has the required access. A personal Cloud environment won't appear in this flow.</li> <li><strong>A coding task won't start</strong>: Ask your admin to confirm that Cloud delegation is available and Codex Cloud is enabled for your workspace. Where Codex Cloud role-based access control is enabled, check that both the deployment's service account and your account have Codex Cloud access. Also check your access to the selected environment and its repositories.</li> <li><strong>Different environment needed</strong>: Start a new conversation and name the repository or shared environment you want to use.</li> <li><strong>Task controls unavailable</strong>: The <strong>Follow along</strong> and <strong>Cancel</strong> controls depend on the deployment's configuration and are intended for the requester.</li> <li><strong>Long threads</strong>: Summarize the relevant issue, expected outcome, and repository in your latest request so the task has enough context.</li> </ul>"};
